  "solution": {
    "text": "Current drawn from the cell in resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.<br /><br />Therefore, heat produced in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.<br /><br />Heat produced in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.<br /><br />As per question,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math><br /><br />On solving we get,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>40</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mtext>63.25&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>",
